  "body": "### Summary\nOperator device test of 2026-11-17, on build `dev-swift` @ 8c6d70c4 or later, after #998 (#977, #978, #865). The large titles are in place on every main page (Catégories, Favoris, Messages…), and they scroll away without the black bar overlay. But the centred title pill of #978 never shows.\n\n### Feedback (operator, 2026-11-17)\n- **(A)** Recherche has no large title like the other main pages.\n- **(B)** The large title collapses on scroll, but **the pill with the title does not appear** once the title is gone.\n- **(D)** Inside a category (a pushed topic list), a pill centred at the top must say which category this is, for UI consistency.\n\n(B) and (D) are probably one bug: `ScreenTitle.swift` gives pushed lists `.pill` from the start (see GAP-978, #1010), yet no pill shows on the device.\n\n### Scope\n1. Find why the pill is not drawn on the device: `ScreenTitle.swift`, the `.largeThenPill` and `.pill` modes, and their call sites (`RootTabsView.swift:153`, `TopicListView.swift:29`, `ForumSearchView.swift:26`). Fix it for both modes.\n2. Recherche (the 5th tab of #896, and the entry in Plus) gets the large title at landing, then the pill, as the other main pages do. Update GAP-978 through the PR's `### Ledger` (`gap-edit`).\n3. A category list shows the category's name in the pill. A tap shows the full title, a long press copies it (#978).\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Main pages: the large title at landing, then the pill once it has collapsed. The same on Recherche.\n- [ ] A pushed category list: the pill with the category name.\n- [ ] A test that fails without the fix, at least on the mode → visibility rule. The device check goes to the general review (#893).\n\n### Related\n#977, #978, #865, PR #998, GAP-978 (#1010), #896.",
